  "sanitisation": "machine account-domain SID rewritten to the bundle placeholder domain 1000000001-1000000002-1000000003 by rewrite_sid_domain.py (in scripts/) (log docs/reviews/case4-sid-rewrite-log-2026-10-20.md); host and operator names rewritten by scrub_public_identifiers.py (in scripts/); the fabricated stale SID S-1-5-21-17630000-17630001-17630002-91763 is not a machine SID and is unchanged; nothing else altered; in the prepare, final and part-D copies every netsh output key 'text' is renamed 'netsh_text' (values unchanged) because the bundle lock reserves 'text' for model output",
  "reading": "The group's effect is a property of the token, not of the account. Under an ordinary launch the token carries S-1-5-32-556 marked use-for-deny-only and the engine refuses the add exactly as for a standard user (F, 4 of 4; N1, 3 of 3; the operator's filtered administrator token, S, 3 of 3). Under a batch logon through a scheduled task the token carries the group enabled (attributes 0x7, elevation type 1, no linked token, integrity medium-plus, session 0, Administrators absent) and the same FwpmFilterAdd0 and FwpmFilterDeleteByKey0 succeed, 3 of 3, nothing left behind: the engine's ACE for the group, (A;;0x307ff;;;NO), applies to that token as Microsoft documents. The over-the-shoulder elevation prompt does not offer a non-administrator its own full token on this build (4 refusals), so the route to the enabled token was a logon that is not split, created by hand.",
